    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I apologize for any confusion caused by my previous responses. Let's clarify the citation rules for you:\n\nIn APA 7th style, for a source with five authors, you would list all five authors in the in-text citation every time you reference that source, like this: (Smith, Johnson, Williams, Brown, & Davis, 2020). However, if you have a source with more than two authors, you would list the first author followed by \"et al.\" in subsequent citations, like this: (Smith et al., 2020).\n\nIn Chicago style, for a source with five authors, you would list all five authors in the in-text citation every time you reference that source, like this: (Smith, Johnson, Williams, Brown, & Davis, 2020). Similar to APA, if you have a source with more than two authors, you would list the first author followed by \"et al.\" in subsequent citations, like this: (Smith et al., 2020).\n\nI hope this provides the clear and professional guidance you need for your PhD paper. If you have any more questions or need further clarification, please feel free to ask. Good luck with your submission!",
